native ISA (aarch64) gets HVF acceleration. amd64 guests fall back to
TCG, which will not reliably clear the existing plan's §8.2 (≤30s
time-to-login) acceptance gate ON THE BUILD HOST itself — building a
baseline whose own gates fail in the build environment is muri.
aarch64-on-aarch64 under HVF clears §8.2 trivially, matches the fleet's
existing aarch64 substrate (every fbrpi node, every Pi 5 / RK3588
target, the fbuild VM, all gitea-release artifact naming), and
satisfies the soft 'phase 1 = both RK3588 + Pi 5' signal at lowest
weight (per feedback_no_projection.md — soft signal, not directive).
amd64 is NOT discarded: the existing PHASE-1-FORGE-TINY-BASELINE amd64
cross-build path becomes the second leg of the same Phase I, tested on
a KVM-capable x86 host (Vultr instance or fleet x86 box) so its gates
have a fair chance to pass. Verified facts only — every qemu-binary
and tool-presence claim used in the matrix is either absolute-path
